  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting, 10-day verified reports, and 48-hour customer notice. S2 keeps the 55°C test and 5% permanent cap, but allows a 24-month corrective-action window without an interim cap and gives per-model results to buyers and regulators but not the public. S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and a six-year retrofit with a feasibility alternative; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt customer notices."
